{"results":[{"url":"https://www.peoplespolicyproject.org/tag/capital/page/2/","final_url":"https://www.peoplespolicyproject.org/tag/capital/page/2/","title":"People's Policy Project","description":"A think tank for the development of an economic system that serves the many, not the few.","language":"en","text":"# Tag: Capital\n\n* # How Should We Understand Capital Income Inequality?\n\n  Public ownership of capital is an important part of reducing inequality.\n* # Wealth Inequality Across Age and Class in 2019\n\n  The top 10 percent of ever age group owns almost all the group's wealth.\n* # Wealth Inequality Across Education and Class in 2019\n\n  Every age and education group has the same sort of inequality.\n* # Wealth Inequality Across Race and Class in 2019\n\n  Wealth continues to be heavily concentrated at the top.\n* # Millionaires and Billionaires Own 79% of All Household Wealth\n\n  The wealthiest among us owns almost everything, once again.\n* # More Bizarre Arguments About the COVID Economic Response\n\n  ProPublica got snowed. It happens to the best of us, even David Dayen.\n* # A Bizarre Argument About the COVID Economic Response\n\n  Is cutting interest rates really a corporate giveaway?\n* # The Racial Wealth Gap Is About the Upper Classes\n\n  The top decile disparities drive almost the entire racial wealth gap.\n* # How To Think About Corporate Bailouts Correctly\n\n  Get that equity. Get that bread. Get those bands. Now. Now. Now.\n* # Some Economic Responses to the Coronavirus Recession\n\n  Some thoughts on how to respond to this recession in particular.\n* # Fareed Zakaria Is Completely Ignorant About the Nordics\n\n  Zakaria fakes his way through another essay with predictable results.\n* # Bloomberg Is Wealthier Than The Bottom 125 Million Americans\n\n  Other estimates suggest the real number is over 150 million people.\n* # Finland's Economy Really Is Highly Socialized\n\n  It is not just ordinary capitalism with a big welfare state. It's more.\n* # The UBI Already Exists. It Is Just Unevenly Distributed.\n\n  Capitial's share provides more than enough money to finance a universal basic income.\n* # Labour's Inclusive Ownership Funds Should Be Fine\n\n  The Financial Times forecasts doom and gloom where there isn't any.\n* # Don’t Blame the Alaska Permanent Fund Dividend\n\n  The state can easily close solve its budget woes with ordinary taxes.\n* # Top 1% Up $21 Trillion. Bottom 50% Down $900 Billion.\n\n  America is a hideously unequal place with a large propertyless underclass.\n* # The Difficulty of Using the Firm in Socialist Policy\n\n  Firm boundaries are arbitrary, which complicates firm-based socialism.\n* # Bernie Sanders Gives the Nod to Funds Socialism\n\n  A Meidner plan for America. Here we go. Here we fucking go!\n* # Fresh Support for Social Wealth Fund Development\n\n  Roosevelt Institute has kind words to say about Inclusive Ownership Funds.","author":null,"published_date":"2020-12-10","latency_ms":4138.546217000112,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}